ndling (no pending-set check). The plan's Tests line says 'integration over the fixture repo through the CLI (the layer the op is used at)', and the acceptance criterion says 'every classification is reachable from the CLI on a fixture'. The shared `classify_commit` carries most of the value. Still, the CLI layer is exercised for `uncovered` only, and `classify_pending` for pr-covered, uncovered and unknown. Either drive the classifications through `classify_pending` or the CLI with a fragment per fixture, or record why the lib layer is the deliberate test seam.", "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "The tail half trusts every verify-resolutions edge as fix-only", "recommendation": "The plan already lists this inference for the boundary review. A `verify-resolutions` interval is the delta since the prior review fact, and the exit-2 widening refusal bounds it but does not make it zero, so new work can ride a verify pass after the cumulative and still read `pr-covered`. No action is wanted at this chunk. Chunk 02's cumulative should rule on it.", "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "'writes nothing' is slightly overstated", "recommendation": "The op reaches `gates._tree_key_fn`, which persists the clone-shared `tree_key_memo`. That is the same cache write `check-cumulative-critic` and the other ephemeral-safe gates make, and it outlives the worktree, so the `_EPHEMERAL_SAFE_COMMANDS` membership is right. Only the plan's stated reason is loose. No edit is wanted.", "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "record-lint chunk-ref-missing: unchecked", "recommendation": "chunk-ref-missing graded chunk 01 of .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-boundary-coverage-check.md: chunk 01 was inferred as the plan's first open chunk (`plan_status.current_chunks`) because the dispatch carried no chunk \u2014 a chunk whose review is not yet recorded is still open, so this may be the next chunk rather than the reviewed one", "source":